// Human body plan v2 (plan §2.6, §4A.3; docs/specs/phase4/anatomy-and-body-plans.md 3.2 and 3.3).
// Relative part sizes are DF's (upper body 18%, lower body 18%, head 5.4%, neck 1.8%, upper arm 3.6%, lower arm 3.6%, hand 1.4%,
// upper leg 9%, lower leg 7.2%, foot 2.2%; sided parts exist left and right). The 10 base ids and 16 instances of v1 stay; v2 adds
// 12 hosted base ids (19 instances: eyes, ears, nose, skull, jaw, teeth, ribs, collarbones, pelvis, kneecaps, thumbs, fingers) for 35.
// skull, ribs and pelvis are "shell" parts: the host's bone layer promoted to a part (it keeps the bone layer in the host's stack).
// Structures sit inside the muscle and are rolled by area when the muscle is cut: vessels and tendons (v1), a motor and a sensory
// nerve per limb section (v1's single nerve split 50/50, migrated below), ligaments at the six joints, the spinal cord in the neck,
// upper and lower body (reached mostly from behind: facing_pm). gap_boost multiplies the area when an aimed blow bypassed the
// armour at that named gap. Layer thicknesses (mm), area fractions and bleed rates are estimates; bleed numbers follow plan §4A.3.
[
{
 "type": "body_plan", "id": "human", "name": "Human", "size_cm3": 70000, "blood_ml": 5000, "blood_ml_per_kg": 71, "tissue_set": "human",
 "parts": [
  { "id": "upper_body", "name": "Upper body", "relative_size": 0.18, "depth_mm": 200, "rib_slip": true,
